# pstack workflow (trial)

Trial through 2026-12-03 (RUB-605); Ruben decides keep or revert.

Follow [pstack](https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack) principles (Lauren Tan / poteto) on every change:

- **subtract-before-you-add** — remove dead weight first, then build on the simpler base
- **fix-root-causes** — fix the first place the system went wrong; a guard is a fix only when the state it handles is legitimate
- **prove-it-works** — before declaring done, verify against the real artifact (run the feature, read the actual value, inspect the diff), not a proxy, self-report, or "it compiles"
- **minimize-reader-load** — collapse one-caller wrappers and shrink mutable scope; keep diffs easy to review

## Before declaring done

Run the pstack verification step and put the evidence in the PR body:

1. Exercise the changed behavior for real (feature run / mapped journey), not only lint or compile.
2. Run the focused tests that cover the change.
3. Follow the repo verification skill at `.omp/skills/verify-artfct/SKILL.md` and its feature map under `.omp/skills/verify-artfct/features/` when the change touches a mapped journey (or when proving browser / MCP / Worker behavior).

## Artifacts are ARTFCT-only

pstack relies on artifacts (evidence, reports, proofs). This team uses its own artifact system, ARTFCT (artfct.dev, via the Artfct MCP/plugin), and never a third-party artifact store. Proof media goes as hosted artifacts in the PR body, never committed into the branch.
